---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms of Use" description="Terms and conditions for using Coding Shuffle Duel." showBack={true}>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="hero-badge">
      <img src="/icons/book_icon.png" alt="" class="badge-icon" />
      Legal
    </div>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective date: July 1, 2026 · Last updated: July 1, 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-card">
    <p>
      By downloading or using Coding Shuffle Duel ("the App"), you agree to be bound by these
      Terms of Use ("Terms"). Please read them carefully. If you do not agree, do not use the App.
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms constitute a legally binding agreement between you and the Coding Shuffle Duel
      team. By installing or using the App, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree
      to these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Description of the App</h2>
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel is a mobile educational game for Android that teaches programming
      syntax through interactive drag-and-drop puzzles. The App is currently available on
      Android only — iOS and PC versions are planned for future release.
    </p>
    <p>The App provides, among other things:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Campaign Mode</strong> — handcrafted SQL puzzles across difficulty levels.</li>
      <li><strong>SQL Stream Mode</strong> — a fast-paced arcade mode for syntax recognition.</li>
      <li><strong>Survival Mode</strong> — an endless challenge with increasing difficulty.</li>
      <li><strong>Daily Challenge</strong> — one shared puzzle per day for all players.</li>
      <li><strong>XP & Progression</strong> — stars, achievements, and level tracking.</li>
      <li><strong>Offline support</strong> — all core features work without internet connectivity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 13 years of age to use this App. Users under 18 should have parental
      or guardian consent before use. By using the App, you confirm that you meet this requirement.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since no account is required to play, younger users can enjoy the full offline experience
      without providing any personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>4. No Account Required</h2>
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel does not require account creation to use. All gameplay, progress, and
      data are stored locally on your device by default. Account creation is an optional feature
      available solely for the purpose of syncing your progress across devices.
    </p>
    <p>Since there are no mandatory accounts, you are solely responsible for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Maintaining access to your device.</li>
      <li>Understanding that uninstalling the App will permanently delete all local data.</li>
      <li>Backing up your data if desired, via the Settings page or by creating an account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>You may use the App for personal, non-commercial purposes only. You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the App's source code.</li>
      <li>Modify, redistribute, or create derivative works based on the App.</li>
      <li>Use the App to violate any applicable law or regulation.</li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any backend systems or other users' accounts.</li>
      <li>Exploit bugs or glitches to gain an unfair advantage in any game mode.</li>
      <li>Transmit malicious code, spam, or any unauthorized data through the App.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Optional Account & Cloud Sync</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to create an account, you are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality
      of your credentials. You agree to provide accurate information (a valid email address and a
      username of your choosing) and to notify us immediately of any unauthorized use of your account.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your failure to protect your account
      credentials.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Voluntary Support & Ads</h2>
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel is completely free and contains no forced advertising. We offer an
      optional "Support Us" section where you may choose to watch ads as a voluntary way to
      support the development of the game. This feature is entirely opt-in and has no impact on
      gameplay or progression.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel, including its name, logo, design, gameplay systems, and all associated
      content, is owned by the Coding Shuffle Duel team and is protected by copyright and
      intellectual property law.
    </p>
    <p>
      We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the App for personal,
      non-commercial purposes on your Android device. This license does not include the right to
      copy, modify, or distribute any part of the App.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your in-game progress and data remain yours. Since your data is stored locally on your
      device (or in your personal account if you opt in to sync), we do not claim any ownership
      over it.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data & Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Your privacy is important to us. The App is built on an offline-first architecture — no data
      is collected from players who do not create an account. For users who opt in to cloud sync,
      only email, username, and game progress are stored.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please review our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for full details. Key points:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>No data is collected without an account.</li>
      <li>We do not share or sell your data to any third party.</li>
      <li>You can delete your data at any time from the Settings page.</li>
      <li>Uninstalling the App permanently deletes all local data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      The App is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, express or
      implied. We do not guarantee that the App will be error-free, uninterrupted, or compatible
      with all Android devices. Educational content is provided for informational purposes and
      does not constitute professional instruction or certification.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Coding Shuffle Duel team shall not
      be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from your
      use of the App, including but not limited to loss of data, loss of progress, or device
      compatibility issues. Our total liability shall not exceed the amount you paid for the App,
      which is currently free.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Data Loss</h2>
    <p>
      Since all data is stored locally on your device by default, we cannot recover lost data
      under any circumstances. Device issues, accidental uninstallation, or clearing app data
      will result in permanent loss of local progress. We strongly recommend creating an account
      to enable cloud sync if your progress is important to you.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Modifications to the App & Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We reserve the right to update, modify, or discontinue the App or any of its features at
      any time. We may also update these Terms — the effective date at the top of this page will
      reflect any changes. Continued use of the App after an update constitutes your acceptance
      of the revised Terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since the App is offline-first, updates are optional. Previous versions will continue to
      function on your device even if new versions are released.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Termination</h2>
    <p>
      Since no account is required to play, there is nothing to terminate for most users. You
      can stop using the App at any time by uninstalling it. If you have an account and violate
      these Terms, we reserve the right to suspend or terminate your account access.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of Tunisia, without regard to conflict of law principles.
      Any disputes arising from these Terms or your use of the App should be resolved through
      good-faith communication via our contact email before any formal proceedings.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Severability</h2>
    <p>
      If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining
      provisions will continue in full force and effect.
    </p>

    <h2>17. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms? We're happy to help.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:codingshuffleduel@gmail.com">codingshuffleduel@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>Acknowledgment</h2>
    <p>By using Coding Shuffle Duel, you acknowledge that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You have read and understood these Terms of Use.</li>
      <li>You agree to be bound by them.</li>
      <li>The App is currently available on Android only; other platforms are planned.</li>
      <li>No account is required — all core features work fully offline.</li>
      <li>Uninstalling the App will permanently delete all local data.</li>
      <li>We do not collect, access, or share your data without your explicit opt-in.</li>
      <li>The voluntary support/ads feature is entirely optional and affects nothing in-game.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .badge-icon {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    object-fit: contain;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
</style>